{"format_version":1,"partition":29912,"records":{"a-prominenter":{"entries":[["a-prominenter",null,null,"It appears that the earliest use of A-Prominenter versus B-Prominenter was at the Theresienstadt Ghetto (where since 1942 the SS sent Jews to be treated comparatively mildly, including especially celebrities and decorated WWI veterans). A-Prominente were recognized as celebrities by the SS directly, whereas B-Prominente were proposed by the inmates’ council.\nTo what (if any) degree the contemporary use of the terms continues the above terminology would have to be shown by in-depth study.",{"w":"A-Prominenter","g":"m"}]],"senses":[[685115,"a-prominenter","noun","A-list celebrity (very widely known and respected person)",0,"m"]]},"abgebt":{"entries":[["abgebt",null,null,null]],"senses":[[90215,"abgebt","verb","second-person plural dependent present of abgeben",0]],"inflections":[["abgebt","abgeben","indicative,plural,present,second-person,subordinate-clause"]]},"bruderhofes":{"entries":[["bruderhofes",null,"[ˈbruːdɐˌhoːfəs]",null]],"senses":[[699089,"bruderhofes","noun","genitive singular of Bruderhof",0]],"inflections":[["bruderhofes","bruderhof","genitive"]]},"bullösem":{"entries":[["bullösem",null,null,null]],"senses":[[458900,"bullösem","adj","strong dative masculine/neuter singular of bullös",0]],"inflections":[["bullösem","bullös","dative,masculine,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"goldartiges":{"entries":[["goldartiges",null,null,null]],"senses":[[245375,"goldartiges","adj","strong/mixed nominative/accusative neuter singular of goldartig",0]],"inflections":[["goldartiges","goldartig","neuter,nominative,singular,strong,without-article"]]},"instanz":{"entries":[["instanz",null,null,"Learned borrowing from Latin īnstantia (“perseverence, urgency”), first referring to the pursuit of a legal matter, then the office responsible for that pursuit. The technological sense is a later semantic loan from English instance.",{"g":"f","decl":"||||en|en|en|en"}]],"sense